{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '430,480p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md\"","aggregated_output":"because both lowerers copy that flag and infer nothing. Lifted and unlifted\nprograms must be compared under an explicit arity caveat, and the B0\nnormalizer applies to whichever named AST the lowerer receives. This VM\nneither depends on nor forbids those stages.\n\nThe verified identity documentation is:\n\n    https://www.unison-lang.org/docs/the-big-idea/\n    https://unison-lang.org/whats-new/writeup-of-our-first-unison-meetup\n\nThe verified runtime documentation and source directory are:\n\n    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unisonweb/unison/trunk/\n      unison-runtime/src/Unison/Runtime/docs.markdown\n    https://github.com/unisonweb/unison/tree/trunk/\n      unison-runtime/src/Unison/Runtime\n\nUNVERIFIED here: evaluation as a documented pipeline stage, the detailed\ncomponent listing, whether the runtime input is the stored identity artifact,\nreference resolution, MCode and Machine semantics, and whether\n`docs.markdown` is current.\n\n### 7.2 Future reference-by-hash linking as a stream topology\n\nReference-by-hash is a later epic, not B-phase VM machinery. The linker is a\nprocess between streams: it consumes executable images and a\nvalue-held name environment, uses the projection fingerprint only as a lookup\nindex, emits verified definition requests, consumes definition datoms,\nand emits a linked image or an explicit refusal. This follows the axiom that\nall IO and data flow through append-only streams. No global mutable registry\nis introduced, and no direct function-to-function call crosses the boundary.\nThe boundary is `dao.stream`; local and remote resolution are the same\ntransport-neutral mechanism, and their physical placement is not a linker\ndecision.\n\n`yin.vm.content` verifies content-addressed rows and vectors. `load-vector`\nrecords the `jing/segment-key` in `:code-aliases`; `:yin.code/hash` is the\nbatch attribute checked when loading an image. `yin.vm.completion` computes\nconservative named-VM closure facts and `:yin.k/requires`, including reachable\nsegments, stores, parked records, primitives, and modules. None rewrites a\nfree name to a definition hash, and the completion adapter is not yet a\nde Bruijn adapter.\n\nA future linked dimension may contain `:call-hash H`. If `H` is unavailable,\nthe linked interpreter must park its explicit continuation and emit a request\nrecord on a request stream. A definition-arrival consumer reads datoms from a\nresponse stream, verifies their content address through `yin.vm.content`,\nloads them, and resumes the parked continuation. The request token, parked\ncontinuation, and response are data; no callback is retained. Gaps, timeouts,\nand permanent absence remain explicit stream outcomes. The request convention,\narrival consumer, and name-environment stream are new.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '480,510p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '480,510p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md\"","aggregated_output":"arrival consumer, and name-environment stream are new.\n\nCycles are decided here as a linker principle: mutually recursive definitions\nform one strongly connected component, whose members are ordered by canonical\nimage hash before the component hash is computed. Authority\nalso remains a decision: a name environment needs a declared ledger, trust,\nand provenance. Verification is supplied by Jing and the loader, while the\nlinked consumer must reject absent or mismatched content before execution.\nStreams provide failure events but do not choose retry or terminal policy.\n\nThis does not require a semantic change to B0 through B5. B3 already makes\nloading and continuation state explicit, and B4 carries park and resume as\ndata transitions. The VM accepts loaded images only as values in its state and\nnever invokes a loader; absence is a park plus a request emission. B6 is the\nadditive phase for request and response streams, the\nlinked dimension, `:call-hash`, cycle handling, and failure policy.\n\nCompletion requires hash-address loading, cycle-safe manifests, explicit\nauthority, gap and timeout outcomes, malformed or missing-address diagnostics,\nand differential tests showing named and linked images agree where the name\nenvironment is fixed. It must not alter the projection fingerprint. It does\nnot establish global distribution or any property of the Unison runtime,\nwhich is UNVERIFIED here.\n\n### 7.3 Lossless source view non-goal\n\nThe VM does not build a second lossless record DAG. Named datoms remain the\nlossless source, and lexical positions, binder diagnostics, and provenance are\nderived into the executable image as needed. A separate inverse view would\nrequire its own design and is outside B0 through B6.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
